1219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 764 0 R
/E (Both 1-cyclopropylbutane and butylcyclopropane refer to the same structure, but they differ in their choice of parent structure and naming. The correct IUPAC name is 1-cyclopropylbutane because the longest acyclic chain contains four carbon atoms, while the cyclopropane ring contains only three. According to the parent structure selection rule, the acyclic chain is chosen as the parent when it contains more carbon atoms than the ring; thus, butane is the parent and cyclopropyl is the substituent)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
